78 #edb/ref 17592186432645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432682 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bb60e818-0b8f-5548-8ae0-4c03ecdde68e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432683 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432683 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432683 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186432599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432683 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c95ca100-3984-5a97-9a0d-82d238cb72cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432684 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432684 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432684 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432684 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432684 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432684 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432684 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432684 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186432601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432684 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cc13ac3c-08d2-5ebd-90fb-f6bd2706df71" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432685 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432604 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432685 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432685 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432685 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432685 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432685 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432685 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432685 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186432604 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432685 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ecdcf851-bd5a-52f8-bfcc-45e6d82c2328" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432686 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432686 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107888" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432686 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432686 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following integrals are equivalent to $Γ(z)$ for $\\text{Re}(z)>0?$\n\nI. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z-1}}{{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432686 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0d9f5142-140d-5b22-b957-299741979b12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432686 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\nΓ(z)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\text{Re}(z)>0.\n$$\n\nWith this definition in mind, let's consider each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral I matches the definition:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=Γ(z)\n$$\n\n- Integral II matches the definition:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z-1}}{{e}^{t}}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=Γ(z)\n$$\n\n- Integral III does *not* match the definition. The lower bound of integration does not match that given in the definition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432687 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432687 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107862" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432687 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432687 #edb/ref 1071 "$Γ(\\frac{1}{2})+4\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432687 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0fdfcf02-67ae-5263-baa1-a6ba5d9b1b6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432687 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=\\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2})=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\pi }=\\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nΓ(\\frac{1}{2})+4\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }+4\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }=4\\sqrt{\\pi }.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432688 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432688 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107833" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432688 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432688 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following integrals are equivalent to $Γ(z)$ for $\\text{Re}(z)>0?$\n\nI. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{{t}^{z-1}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z-1}}{{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}t}{{t}^{1-z}{e}^{t}}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432688 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2346f7c5-c1ac-509c-ac43-d1a23908e3df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432688 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\nΓ(z)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\text{Re}(z)>0.\n$$\n\nWith this definition in mind, let's consider each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral I does *not* match the definition. The integrand $\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{t}^{z-1}}$ is not equivalent to that shown in the definition.\n\n- Integral II does *not* match the definition.  The lower bound of integration does not match that given in the definition.\n\n- Integral III matches the definition:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}t}{{t}^{1-z}{e}^{t}}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=Γ(z)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432689 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432689 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107886" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432689 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432689 #edb/ref 1071 "$Γ(\\frac{7}{2})+Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432689 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "38540fee-f0e4-596e-9eff-9715fa0a19af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432689 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(\\frac{7}{2}) & =\\frac{5}{2}\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\,Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{8}\\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nΓ(\\frac{7}{2})+Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{15}{8}\\sqrt{\\pi }+\\sqrt{\\pi }=\\frac{23}{8}\\sqrt{\\pi }.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432690 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432690 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107829" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432690 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432690 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following integrals are equivalent to $Γ(z)$ for $\\text{Re}(z)>0?$\n\nI. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{{t}^{1-z}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432690 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "43b66f9d-fca5-54ae-b724-0bc204fa830b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432690 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\nΓ(z)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\text{Re}(z)>0.\n$$\n\nWith this definition in mind, let's consider each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral I matches the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{{t}^{1-z}}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=Γ(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Integral II does *not* match the definition. The lower bound of integration does not match that given in the definition.\n\n- Integral III does *not* match the definition. The integrand ${t}^{z-1}{e}^{t}$ is not equivalent to that shown in the definition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432691 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432691 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107848" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432691 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432691 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $Γ(3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432691 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "58e93e99-d92a-5ce1-a5e1-f2a7ff45e177" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432691 #edb/ref 1074 "For any natural number $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\nΓ(n)=(n-1)!.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nΓ(3)=2!=2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432692 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432692 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107855" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432692 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432692 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $4\\sqrt{\\pi }\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432692 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6bbc8ec2-1cd6-5115-ab81-c2fbacd13746" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432692 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(\\frac{5}{2}) & =\\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{\\pi }}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n4\\sqrt{\\pi }\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=4\\sqrt{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }=3\\pi .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432693 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432693 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107832" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432693 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432693 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following integrals are equivalent to $Γ(z)$ for $\\text{Re}(z)>0?$\n\nI. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{t}^{z-1}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z}}{t{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432693 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8aae46a7-7405-5484-9202-26c3555ea95d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432693 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\nΓ(z)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\text{Re}(z)>0.\n$$\n\nWith this definition in mind, let's consider each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral I does *not* match the definition. The integrand $\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{t}^{z-1}}$ is not equivalent to that shown in the definition.\n\n- Integral II matches the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z}}{t{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=Γ(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Integral III matches the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=Γ(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432694 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432694 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107853" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432694 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432694 #edb/ref 1071 "$Γ(45)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432694 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8f3249d6-edac-5050-9528-d13b2bdbb793" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432694 #edb/ref 1074 "For any natural number $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\nΓ(n)=(n-1)!\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nΓ(45)=44!\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432695 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432695 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107860" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432695 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432695 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\,Γ(\\frac{9}{2}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432695 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bd01511b-f45a-5cd4-b173-d099f3266062" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432695 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\,Γ(\\frac{9}{2}) & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot Γ(\\frac{7}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}Γ(\\frac{5}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\  & =7\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432696 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432696 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107845" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432696 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432696 #edb/ref 1071 "$Γ(27)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432696 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cb5b08f1-b473-53d8-ae61-be733c058e2d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432696 #edb/ref 1074 "For any natural number $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\nΓ(n)=(n-1)!\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nΓ(27)=26!\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432697 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432697 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107849" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432697 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432697 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $Γ(6).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432697 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d0d87553-dab1-5046-8598-8f79d15fc0d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432697 #edb/ref 1074 "For any natural number $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\nΓ(n)=(n-1)!.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nΓ(6)=5!=120.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432698 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432698 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107838" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432698 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432698 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following integrals are equivalent to $Γ(z)$ for $\\text{Re}(z)>0?$\n\nI. $3{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{3z-1}}{{e}^{{t}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nII. $3{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{3z-3}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nIII. $3{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{t}^{3z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432698 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ef7933ca-459a-5897-8c5b-5b08b877b68b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432698 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\nΓ(z)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\text{Re}(z)>0.\n$$\n\nWith this definition in mind, let's consider each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral I matches the definition. We use a substitution $s={t}^{3},$ then $3{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t=\\text{d}s.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{3z-1}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{3(z-1)+2}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{3(z-1)}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}(3{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{s}^{z-1}{e}^{-s}\\,\\text{d}s=Γ(z).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Integral II does *not* match the definition. The integrand ${t}^{3z-3}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}$ is not equivalent to that shown in the definition.\n\n- Integral III does *not* match the definition. The lower bound of integration does not match that given in the definition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
